   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "The mass of a bacteria culture is M(t) milligrams at time t hours. Selected values of M(t) are given in the table. Compute the average rate of change of M over each of the intervals \\( [1, 1.100] \\), \\( [1, 1.010] \\), \\( [1, 1.001] \\), and use them to find the rate at which M is changing at \\( t = 1 \\). Indicate units of measure.",
      "command_verb": "estimate"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 9,
      "units": "milligrams per hour"
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The average rate over \\( [1, 1 + h] \\) is \\( \\frac{M(1 + h) - M(1)}{h} \\), which for h = 0.1, 0.01 and 0.001 gives 9.300, 9.030, 9.003.",
         "rule_named": "average rate of change"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "As the intervals shrink the averages approach 9, so the instantaneous rate at \\( t = 1 \\) is 9 milligrams per hour. Each average is only an approximation of it.",
         "mathjson": 9,
         "rule_named": "instantaneous rate as the limit of average rates"
      }
   ],
